{
  "title": { "zh": "谁闯进来了", "en": "What slipped through?" },
  "intro": [
    {
      "t": {
        "zh": "图像对齐后，大的缺口和小的读数波动都还留在差值图里。质检台需要给出明确的超差标记，也要把变化大小保留下来供复核。 <wiki-ref to=\"decision-evidence\"></wiki-ref>",
        "en": "After alignment, both defects and small reading fluctuations remain in the difference image. The station must mark readings beyond tolerance and retain the measured changes for review. <wiki-ref to=\"decision-evidence\"></wiki-ref>"
      }
    }
  ],
  "after": {
    "zh": "\\[M(x,y)=\\begin{cases}1,&D(x,y)>\\tau\\\\0,&D(x,y)\\le\\tau\\end{cases}\\]\n\nD 是对齐后的差异大小，τ 是给定容差。差异图回答“改变了多少”，标记 M 回答“是否超过标准”；相等时不标记。结论仍依赖正确对应、光照条件和容差规范。 <wiki-ref to=\"decision-evidence\"></wiki-ref>",
    "en": "\\[M(x,y)=\\begin{cases}1,&D(x,y)>\\tau\\\\0,&D(x,y)\\le\\tau\\end{cases}\\]\n\nD is aligned difference magnitude and τ the supplied tolerance. D answers how much changed; M answers whether it exceeds the specification. Equality is unmarked. The decision still depends on correspondence, lighting and the tolerance specification. <wiki-ref to=\"decision-evidence\"></wiki-ref>"
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "v0_inspection",
      "kind": "circuit",
      "step": {
        "zh": "按规范标记",
        "en": "Apply the criterion"
      },
      "brief": {
        "zh": "容差由质检规范给定。输出对齐差异，以及严格超过容差的变化标记（1）；其余为 0。",
        "en": "Tolerance is supplied by the inspection specification. Output aligned differences and a 1 only where a difference strictly exceeds tolerance."
      },
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "observed", "label": { "zh": "观测", "en": "Observation" } },
        { "name": "reference", "label": { "zh": "参照", "en": "Reference" } },
        { "name": "d", "type": "vector", "label": { "zh": "取样偏移 d", "en": "Read offset d" } },
        { "name": "tolerance", "label": { "zh": "允许变化", "en": "Tolerance" } }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        { "name": "changes", "label": { "zh": "变化证据", "en": "Change evidence" } },
        { "name": "mask", "label": { "zh": "超差标记", "en": "Over-tolerance mask" } }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "inputs": {
            "observed": [[0.1, 0.4, 0.8, 0.3]],
            "reference": [[0.55, 0.8, 0.3, 0]],
            "d": { "x": 1, "y": 0 },
            "tolerance": 0.1
          },
          "expect": { "changes": [[0.15000000000000002, 0, 0, 0]], "mask": [[1, 0, 0, 0]] }
        },
        {
          "inputs": {
            "observed": [[0.2, 0.6], [0.8, 0.1], [0.4, 0.5]],
            "reference": [[0.15, 0], [0.2, 0.6], [0.8, 0.1]],
            "d": { "x": 0, "y": -1 },
            "tolerance": 0.1
          },
          "expect": { "changes": [[0.15, 0], [0, 0], [0, 0]], "mask": [[1, 0], [0, 0], [0, 0]] }
        },
        {
          "inputs": {
            "observed": [[0.625, 0.25, 0.875]],
            "reference": [[0.5, 0.5, 0.5]],
            "d": { "x": 0, "y": 0 },
            "tolerance": 0.25
          },
          "expect": { "changes": [[0.125, 0.25, 0.375]], "mask": [[0, 0, 1]] }
        }
      ],
      "hidden": [
        {
          "inputs": {
            "observed": [[0.3, 0.7, 0.1], [0.2, 0.9, 0.5]],
            "reference": [[0.15, 0.3, 0.7], [0, 0.2, 0.9]],
            "d": { "x": -1, "y": 0 },
            "tolerance": 0.1
          },
          "expect": { "changes": [[0.15, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0]], "mask": [[1, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0]] }
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "s = shift(observed,d)",
        "change = arithmetic[op=sub](s,reference)",
        "c = abs(change)",
        "m = less(tolerance,c)",
        "changes <- c",
        "mask <- m"
      ],
      "naive": [
        "s = shift(observed,d)",
        "change = arithmetic[op=sub](s,reference)",
        "c = abs(change)",
        "m = less(c,tolerance)",
        "changes <- c",
        "mask <- m"
      ],
      "naiveWhy": {
        "zh": "标记应当随变化超过容差而出现，不是把合格位置标为缺陷。",
        "en": "Mark changes exceeding tolerance, not positions that remain within it."
      },
      "hint": [
        {
          "zh": "先检查差异输出，再检查比较的两个输入谁在前。小于元件在 a<b 时输出 1。",
          "en": "Check the difference first, then the order of the comparison inputs. Less returns 1 when a<b."
        }
      ],
      "sample": {
        "inputs": {
          "observed": {
            "size": [32, 24],
            "base": 0,
            "layers": [
              { "shape": "disc", "cx": 10, "cy": 11, "r": 6, "v": 0.6 },
              { "shape": "rect", "x": 22, "y": 5, "w": 8, "h": 14, "v": 0.8 },
              { "shape": "rect", "x": 24, "y": 10, "w": 3, "h": 4, "v": 0.2 }
            ]
          },
          "reference": {
            "size": [32, 24],
            "base": 0,
            "layers": [
              { "shape": "disc", "cx": 9, "cy": 11, "r": 6, "v": 0.6 },
              { "shape": "rect", "x": 21, "y": 5, "w": 8, "h": 14, "v": 0.8 }
            ]
          },
          "d": { "x": 1, "y": 0 }
        }
      },
      "carry": "0-2"
    }
  ]
}
